    "section_A_which_envelope_is_defensible": "NO GLOBAL UNCONDITIONED PREFIX ENVELOPE IS STATISTICALLY DEFENSIBLE FOR TRAJECTORY COVERAGE. While q90 achieves 84.2%-87.2% pointwise coverage, its simultaneous trajectory coverage is only 67.77% [95% CI: 62.3%, 72.9%]. Calling it '90% reliable' is refuted. q80 and q85 fail both pointwise (67%-78%) and simultaneous (50%-58%) criteria.",
    "section_B_achievability_of_simultaneous_coverage": "Simultaneous trajectory coverage >= 90% is NOT ACHIEVABLE with unconditioned static prefix envelopes without excessive conservatism. Achieving 90% simultaneous coverage requires either static q10's 1,740 Wh/m2 buffer (+38% fuel penalty) or split-conformal inflation to 3,852 Wh/m2.",
    "section_C_closed_loop_recommendation": "DO NOT proceed with an unconditioned global prefix envelope. The prefix formulation is physically valid, but requires regime conditioning (clear vs overcast, or season) before closed-loop testing, because unconditioned bounds collapse in Summer (33.7% simultaneous coverage) while over-buffering Winter (100% coverage).",
